  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance to the Government of Bangladesh in Strengthening the Responses to Human Trafficking</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a joint initiative of the UNODC and the Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of Bangladesh. The project aims to assist the Government of Bangladesh in preventing human trafficking through effective and strengthened law enforcement capacities and by providing protection and assistance to trafficked victims through establishment of national referral mechanisms and increased cooperation between the criminal justice system and civil society. Over a two-year period, the project seeks to: (i) Train law enforcement officials and public prosecutors in victim identification, investigation, prosecution of labor trafficking offenses and referrals for appropriate treatment and reintegration of labor trafficking survivors; (ii) Strengthen and Operationalise specialized Anti Human Trafficking Units to address trafficking with a focus on labor exploitation; (iii) Carry out a country assessment on the current situation of victim support providers; (iv) Develop guidelines for setting up a national referral mechanism for improved civil society and law enforcement cooperation; and (v) Provide protection services for adult male trafficking victims.</narrative>
  </description>
